### 5. Explanation
CATEGORY: high latency
CAUSE: An artificial delay of about 200 ms is configured on the directly connected veth link between ns1 and ns2.
EVIDENCE: rtt min/avg/max/mdev = 180.148/198.350/219.077/12.763 ms with 10 packets transmitted, 10 received, 0% packet loss
EXPLANATION: Ns1 and ns2 are directly connected, so replies should normally arrive in under a millisecond. Here every reply takes around 200 milliseconds while none are lost. That consistent extra waiting time means the delay was added by configuration, not by distance or broken hardware.
